# The qml6-module-* entries below are QML imports resolved by name at runtime:
# dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see them, and Debian ships every QML module as its own
# binary package.  plasma5support backs WindowModel and PowerSource, which
# main.qml instantiates unconditionally, so without it the root item fails to
# create and the desktop draws no wallpaper at all.  QtWebChannel backs the web
# wallpaper bridge.  QtMultimedia (video-backend fallback) and QtWebEngine (web
# backend) are optional at runtime, hence Recommends.  There is no `qt6-webengine`
# binary package in Debian -- the QML module is qml6-module-qtwebengine.
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 plasma-workspace,
 libkf6notifications6,
 libkf6crash6,
 libkf6globalaccel6,
 libkf6i18n6,
 qml6-module-org-kde-plasma-plasma5support,
 qml6-module-qtwebchannel,
Recommends:
 gstreamer1.0-libav,
 qml6-module-qtmultimedia,
 qml6-module-qtwebengine,
 vulkan-tools,
Suggests:
 pipewire-pulse,
Description: Wallpaper Engine integration for KDE Plasma 6
 A wallpaper plugin integrating Wallpaper Engine into KDE Plasma 6
 wallpaper settings. Supports Scene (2D), Web, and Video wallpapers.
 .
 This is a maintained fork with native C++ file operations, fixed
 KDE 6.5+ theme reactivity, and full Plasma 6 / Qt6 support.
 .
 Requires Wallpaper Engine installed on Steam and subscribed Workshop
 wallpapers.
